# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: hz-04-causeway
number: 204
name: Causeway
description: A single-tile bridge over one enormous pit. Nothing can shove you off it — but anything with a pull, on either side, can.
design: Hazard Pressure 4 of 10 — one hole, one bridge.
design: The causeway is one tile wide, so a Stalker can never flank you on it: the tile it would need to stand on is the pit itself. Only a displacement ACROSS the causeway can reach you there, which is what the two Grapplers on the rim are for — and what your Threadcaster does back to anything that steps onto it.

spawn h = Husk
spawn g = Grappler
spawn s = Stalker

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..h.....B
  .^.....BB
  ..OO.OO..
  HgOO.OOgH
  ..OO.OO..
  As.....^.
  AA...h...
